## 10. Build Phases & Milestones

### Phase 1 — Core Binary (Weeks 1–3)

**Goal:** Working MCP server with indexing, file watching, and both tools functional.

| Deliverable | CLIs Served | Done When |
|-------------|-------------|-----------|
| Go module scaffold + CI pipeline | — | Tests pass on PR |
| Language parsers (Go, TS, JS, Python, Rust) | All 6 | Symbols extracted correctly |
| Index store (bbolt or sqlite) | All 6 | Persists and loads correctly |
| File watcher (fsnotify) | All 6 | Changes reflected in < 2s |
| MCP server — stdio transport | All 6 | `query_codebase` returns results |
| MCP server — HTTP transport | All 6 | Same as stdio via HTTP |
| `get_architecture` pre-computation | All 6 | Summary generated on reindex |
| `max-context --index`, `--reindex`, `--status` | All 6 | All commands work correctly |

**Exit criteria:** An agent using the MCP server can query any Go or TypeScript project and get useful symbol results within 200ms.

---

### Phase 2 — Setup Subcommand (Weeks 4–5)

**Goal:** `max-context setup <cli>` works for all 6 CLIs.

| Deliverable | CLIs Served | Done When |
|-------------|-------------|-----------|
| AGENTS.md template + append logic | All 6 | Appends without overwrite |
| `.cursor/mcp.json` writer | Cursor | Config accepted by Cursor |
| `.windsurf/rules/` + workflow writer | Windsurf | Config accepted by Windsurf |
| `.codex/config.toml` writer | Codex | MCP server discovered |
| Antigravity MCP config writer | Antigravity | MCP server discovered |
| `.vscode/mcp.json` writer | VS Code | MCP server discovered |
| `.mcp.json` writer (Claude Code) | Claude Code | MCP server discovered |
| `max-context setup all` | All 6 | All configs written in sequence |
| Idempotency (re-running setup is safe) | All 6 | No duplicate entries |

**Exit criteria:** Running `max-context setup all` on a fresh project produces correct, non-conflicting configs for all 6 CLIs.

